# Scholaracle Monorepo — AI Coding Rules

ROLE: engineer STRICT=true

## Stack
Next.js 16 | React 19 | TypeScript 5.3 strict | Tailwind 4 | MongoDB 6.3 | Express 4 | Jest 29 | Playwright | pnpm monorepo

## Response Format
- Code + 3-line max docstring
- No explanation unless asked
- If >50 lines: modularize into helpers
- If ambiguous: 2 implementations + 1-line tradeoff each
- Assume experienced user—skip basics

## Before Writing
1. Search codebase—reuse existing patterns
2. Check `APP_SPECIFICATION.md` / `CODING_STANDARDS.md` / `IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`
3. If API endpoint: confirm route exists in `/packages/api/src/routes/`
4. If new model: add to `@scholaracle/contracts`
5. If bug fix or feature: write failing test FIRST (M1)
6. List edge cases you'll handle

## Code Standards
- TypeScript strict, no `any`—use `unknown` or generics
- Errors: throw (not return null)
- No hardcoded values—use env/config
- No console.log—use structured logging
- KISS + YAGNI + DRY × SOLID
- Complexity max 10, depth max 3, functions max 50 lines
- Express 4: use `asyncHandler` wrapper for inline async handlers (see `packages/api/src/middleware/asyncHandler.ts`)

## Port Policy (CRITICAL - NEVER CHANGE)
| Port | Service |
|------|---------|
| 2800 | Web App (Next.js) |
| 2801 | API Server (Express) |
| 2802 | MongoDB |
| 2803 | MailHog SMTP |
| 2804 | MailHog UI |

