## E2E User Experience Test Requirements (CRITICAL)

E2E tests verify the FULL user experience through the real browser.

### Architecture: Fail-Fast Pyramid
Tests are organized in dependency layers — if a lower layer fails, higher layers are skipped:

| Layer | Name | Tests | Depends On |
|-------|------|-------|------------|
| 0 | @critical | Health, API, page load | — |
| 1 | @auth | Login, register, logout, password reset | Layer 0 |
| 2 | @dashboard | Parent + admin dashboards | Layer 1 |
| 3 | @navigation | Sidebar, breadcrumbs, routing | Layer 2 |
| 4 | @feature | CRUD operations, filters, settings | Layer 3 |
| 5 | @integration | Cross-feature flows | Layer 4 |
| 6 | @error | Error handling, 404, unauthorized | Layer 5 |
| 7 | @onboarding | Full onboarding wizard UX | Layer 0 |
| 8 | @multi-parent | Multi-parent sharing flows | Layer 0 |

### Seed Data
- Seed route at `packages/api/src/routes/seed/seed.ts` creates all test data
- Guarded by `NODE_ENV !== 'production'`
- Global setup POSTs to `/api/seed?force=true` before all tests
- Seeds: 3 parents, 5 admins, 2 students, 2 alerts, 2 payments, 1 subscription

### Page Object Pattern
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT — raw selectors in tests
await page.click('[data-testid="btn-login"]');
await page.fill('[data-testid="input-email"]', 'user@test.com');

// ✅ REQUIRE — page objects (from packages/e2e/pages/)
import { LoginPage } from '../pages/login.page';
const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);
await loginPage.login('user@test.com', 'password');
```

### E2E Safety Rules
- ALWAYS use `data-testid` selectors (never CSS classes or nth-child)
- ALWAYS use page objects from `packages/e2e/pages/`
- NEVER hardcode credentials — use fixtures from `packages/e2e/fixtures/`
- Test data comes from seed route — never manipulate DB directly in E2E tests

