## Safety Rails
- Never delete/refactor/optimize without OK
- Preserve comments & existing style
- Assume code has purpose
- Present simpler alternative with confidence (1-10) before edits
- Never call paid external APIs in tests — mock all external services
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets
- Stripe webhook tests: mock both repositories via `jest.mock('@scholaracle/database')`

## Self-Check
```
[ ] Tests written FIRST (TDD — M1)
[ ] No placeholder code
[ ] Edge cases handled
[ ] Interfaces are small and focused (ISP — M2)
[ ] Package boundaries respected (M3)
[ ] Repository pattern used, no direct DB access (M4)
[ ] Types from @scholaracle/contracts (M5)
[ ] Zod schema if API input (M8)
[ ] Middleware chain on API routes (M9)
[ ] Factory helpers in tests (M10)
[ ] Async handlers wrapped (M11)
[ ] data-testid on all interactive UI elements
[ ] STRICT mode honored
[ ] Ports unchanged (2800-2804)
```

## Quick Reference
```bash
# Dev commands
pnpm dev                                    # Start all services
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/web dev          # Web only
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/api dev          # API only

# Testing
pnpm test                                   # Jest (all packages)
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/database test    # Single package
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/e2e test         # Playwright E2E

# Type checking
pnpm typecheck                              # All packages

# Linting
pnpm lint                                   # ESLint
pnpm format                                 # Prettier

# Build
pnpm build                                  # Build all packages
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/api... build     # API + transitive deps
```

## Modular Code Structure

### Size Thresholds

| Metric | Limit | Rationale |
|--------|-------|-----------|
| **File Length** | 250 lines max | Package-focused |
| **Function** | 40 lines max | Single responsibility |
| **Component** | 180 lines max | UI boundary |
| **Service** | 200 lines max | Per-package service |
| **Repository** | 150 lines max | Data access focused |
| **Parameters** | 6 max | Use typed objects |
| **Nesting Depth** | 3 levels max | Extract helpers |

### When Limits Are Exceeded
```
If Service > 200 lines:
  → Split by responsibility (Generator, Delivery, Scheduler)
  → Use @scholaracle/interfaces for segregation

If Repository > 150 lines:
  → Split read/write operations (IXxxReader + IXxxWriter)
  → Extract query builders

If Component > 180 lines:
  → Extract into packages/web/components/
  → Use composition with useAsyncData hooks
```

## Violation Response
When violation detected:
1. REJECT with mandate number (M1-M11)
2. Show bad code vs good code
3. Reference relevant package/file
4. Provide fix instruction

## CLI Output
No emojis in: shell scripts, terminal commands, CI/CD, logs, error messages
Allowed in: .md files, React components, code comments

